# configure/networking.md: NETWORK SETTINGS, the Wi-Fi picker, a saved
# network's dialog and SAVED NETWORKS. Needs the stand-in wifictl (README).
# MAIN MENU signed out: NETWORK SETTINGS is the sixth row; on NETWORK
# SETTINGS, WI-FI NETWORK is five presses down from IP ADDRESS and MANAGE
# SAVED NETWORKS two more. In the picker the stand-in lists Home Wi-Fi (in
# use) first and Cafe (saved) third.
key ret
wait-for-change 30 0
settle
key down
wait-for-change 30 0
key down
wait-for-change 30 0
key down
wait-for-change 30 0
key down
wait-for-change 30 0
key down
wait-for-change 30 0
settle
key x
wait-for-change 30 0
settle
shot network-settings
key down
wait-for-change 30 0
key down
wait-for-change 30 0
key down
wait-for-change 30 0
key down
wait-for-change 30 0
key down
wait-for-change 30 0
settle
key x
wait-for-change 30 0
wait 5
settle
shot wifi-networks
key down
wait-for-change 30 0
key down
wait-for-change 30 0
settle
key x
wait-for-change 30 0
settle
shot wifi-saved-network
key z
wait-for-change 30 0
settle
key z
wait-for-change 30 0
settle
key down
wait-for-change 30 0
key down
wait-for-change 30 0
settle
key x
wait-for-change 30 0
wait 3
settle
shot saved-networks
key x
wait-for-change 30 0
settle
shot forget-network
dismiss-dialogs
